PROJECT: Ethiopian School Management System (ESMS)

1. ROLE AND RESPONSIBILITY

Act as a senior software architect, full-stack developer, Android developer, database engineer, UI/UX designer, cybersecurity specialist, and DevOps engineer.

Build a production-ready, secure, scalable, multi-school School Management System for Ethiopia.

Do not create only a demonstration or static prototype. Implement working features, database integration, authentication, authorization, validation, error handling, testing, and deployment documentation.

Work incrementally. Start by analyzing requirements and designing the architecture. Then implement the system module by module, running tests and fixing errors at every stage.

Never claim a feature is complete unless its implementation and tests support that claim.

2. PROJECT OBJECTIVES

The platform must:

- Serve private and government schools in Ethiopia.
- Support multiple schools on one platform.
- Provide web applications and native Android applications.
- Support Amharic and English.
- Work with unreliable internet connections.
- Support cloud hosting and optional local school servers.
- Protect confidential student, parent, teacher, and financial records.
- Generate professional reports in PDF and Excel formats.
- Support Ethiopian Birr (ETB).
- Support Ethiopian and Gregorian calendar display.
- Be responsive on computers, tablets, and Android phones.
- Allow future expansion to additional Ethiopian languages.

